Patchlevel 2, upgrading NetHack to NetHack 3.1.2, was submitted today
to the moderator of comp.sources.games.

pub/NH3.1, the game's archive on linc.cis.upenn.edu, will be updated
only a week or so _after_ Patchlevel 2 appears on comp.sources.games.  So,
please do not bother looking in linc for an advance copy, or for updated
binaries.  They will not be there until they are posted in other
archives.  I'm sure you understand the reasons for this, and I am asking
for your continued cooperation not to load linc with unnecessary, NetHack
related, ftp logins.

We thank the multitude of people who sent suggestions, bug reports, and
proposed patches.  Many of these were imlemented, fixed, and incorporated,
respectively.  Some suggestions came too late for consideration for this
Patchlevel.  They will be considered for the next one.

Now to some of the Pl2 details.  The Amiga and Mac ports have again
changed the most, both in user interface for the previously existing
windowing systems and in adding support for "tty" windowing.  The Amiga and
Mac porting teams have invested extraordinay efforts in their ports'
improvements, and we trust that the results will please you.

The MS-DOS versions may now use direct screen I/O instead of going
through termcap routines, and be compiled for NEC PC-9801 machines thanks
to Yamamoto Keizo.  The SYSV 386 music driver was ported to 386BSD by
Andrew Chernov and SCO by Andreas Arens.

In general news, the pickup and disclosure options were enhanced;
information on the new usage is available from the Guidebook and
intra-game options help.

Many bugs were fixed, of which the most commonly encountered fatal ones
were associated with cursed bags of holding, renaming shopkeepers, objects
falling through trapdoors on deep levels, and kicking embedded objects
loose.

NOTICE:  Bones and save files from previous versions should be discarded
when upgrading to 3.1.2.

For the NetHack Development Team,

-Izchak


